leg before wicket lbw one of ways which batsman can be dismissed sport of cricket following an appeal by fielding side umpire may rule batsman out lbw if ball would have struck wicket but was instead intercepted by any part of batsman body except hand holding bat umpire decision will depend on number of criteria including where ball pitched whether ball hit line with wickets and whether batsman was attempting to hit ball 
