after considerable debate and various experiments law was changed again # an attempt to reduce pad play new version which used to this day allowed batsmen to be out lbw some circumstances if they did not attempt to hit ball with their bat since availability of television replays and later ball tracking technology to assist umpires has increased percentage of lbws major matches however accuracy of technology and consequences of its use remain controversial 
