game intended to make player feel small and to give them sense of about their surroundings basic idea for game as designed by chen was to create game that moved beyond typical defeat kill win mentality of most video games team initially created prototype named dragon that involved players trying to draw away large monster from other players but eventually discarded it after finding it was too easy for players to ignore each other favor of their own objectives 
developers designed game like japanese garden where they attempted to remove all of game elements that did not fit with others so emotions they wanted game to evoke would come through this intended to make game feel intuitive to player so they can explore and feel sense of wonder without direct instructions story arc of game designed to explicitly follow joseph campbell theory of narrative or hero journey so as to enhance emotional connection of players as they journey together his speech chen noted that three of their # had cried upon completing game 
multiplayer component of journey was designed to facilitate cooperation between players without forcing it and without allowing competition it intended to allow players to feel connection to other people through exploring with them rather than talking to them or fighting them plan was to create game where people felt they are connected with each other to show positive side of humanity them developers felt focus on caring about other player would be diluted by too many game elements such as additional goals or tasks as players would focus on those and ignore other player they also felt having text or voice communication between players or showing would allow players biases and to come between them and other player 
